  {
   "id": 23,
   "type": "MarkdownNote",
   "pos": [
    560,
    560
   ],
   "size": [
    330,
    660
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 11,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "title": "How to use",
   "properties": {
    "ue_properties": {
     "widget_ue_connectable": {},
     "version": "7.8",
     "input_ue_unconnectable": {}
    }
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "## H3 image edit, 16 MP — CUDA (int8_convrot)\n\nRenders at 4 MP, upscales 2x in latent space, then refines 16 steps at full size. A one-shot 16 MP render looks fine from a distance but melts at 1:1; this route stays sharp.\n\n1. **Load your images** in Reference 1 (the scene) and Reference 2 (the asset). More references: connect a LoadImage to the next free `ref_image_N` slot on the H3 node (up to 5). For text-to-image, use a flat gray image as the only reference.\n2. **Write the instruction.** Refer to images as `<Picture 1>`, `<Picture 2>`. Shape: `Task: Reference-guided generation.` → what each picture supplies (and does NOT supply) → the edit, with \"exactly one\" → what must stay.\n3. **Base size**: keep 4 MP and match the scene's aspect. The output is twice the width and height (4 MP → ~16 MP).\n4. **Queue.** Base pass: euler/simple, 40 steps. Refine: er_sde, 16 steps. About 10 minutes on an RTX PRO 4500. Result lands in `output/h3_edit/`.\n\nNeeds everything the normal edit workflow needs, plus the latent upscaler pack (github.com/LBH-123-AI/Comfyui_Minimax_h3_latent_Upscaler) and its `minimax_h3_latent_upscaler_3d_bf16.safetensors` in `models/latent_upscale_models`.\n\nLeave groups 3 and 5 alone. `length` must stay 1 — that is what makes the video model render a still."
   ],
   "widgets_values_named": {
    "text": "## H3 image edit, 16 MP — CUDA (int8_convrot)\n\nRenders at 4 MP, upscales 2x in latent space, then refines 16 steps at full size. A one-shot 16 MP render looks fine from a distance but melts at 1:1; this route stays sharp.\n\n1. **Load your images** in Reference 1 (the scene) and Reference 2 (the asset). More references: connect a LoadImage to the next free `ref_image_N` slot on the H3 node (up to 5). For text-to-image, use a flat gray image as the only reference.\n2. **Write the instruction.** Refer to images as `<Picture 1>`, `<Picture 2>`. Shape: `Task: Reference-guided generation.` → what each picture supplies (and does NOT supply) → the edit, with \"exactly one\" → what must stay.\n3. **Base size**: keep 4 MP and match the scene's aspect. The output is twice the width and height (4 MP → ~16 MP).\n4. **Queue.** Base pass: euler/simple, 40 steps. Refine: er_sde, 16 steps. About 10 minutes on an RTX PRO 4500. Result lands in `output/h3_edit/`.\n\nNeeds everything the normal edit workflow needs, plus the latent upscaler pack (github.com/LBH-123-AI/Comfyui_Minimax_h3_latent_Upscaler) and its `minimax_h3_latent_upscaler_3d_bf16.safetensors` in `models/latent_upscale_models`.\n\nLeave groups 3 and 5 alone. `length` must stay 1 — that is what makes the video model render a still."
   },
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
